{"term":"Germany","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:59344778f8e3d05364","definition":"A nation or civilization occupying the country around the Rhine, Elbe, and upper Danube Rivers in Central Europe, taken as a whole under its various governments.","example":"Ancient Germany, excluding from its independent limits the province weſtward of the Rhine, which had ſubmitted to the Roman yoke, extended itſelf over a third part of Europe. Almoſt the whole of modern Germany, Denmark, Norway, Sweden, Finland, Livonia, Pruſſia, and the greater part of Poland, were peopled by the various tribes of one great nation, whoſe complexion, manners, and language, denoted a common origin and preſerved a ſtriking reſemblance.","pos":"name","synonyms":["Deutschland","Germania","Dutchland","Germanland","North German Confederation","German Confederation","Confederation of the Rhine","Holy Roman Empire","First Reich","German Reich","East Francia","Austria"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"countable, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Germany#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:49c3c27cc62d0ff300","definition":"The principal state in this country, including","example":"There had been a long bloody war in the empire of Germany for twelve years, between the Emperor, the Duke of Bavaria, the King of Spain, and the Popiſh Princes and Electors, on the one side; and the Proteſtant Princes on the other; and both ſides having been exhauſted by the war, and even the Catholicks themſelves beginning to diſlike the growing power of the houſe of Auſtria, it was thought that all parties were willing to make peace.","pos":"name","synonyms":["Deutschland","Germania","Dutchland","Germanland","North German Confederation","German Confederation","Confederation of the Rhine","Holy Roman Empire","First Reich","German Reich","East Francia","Austria"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"countable, historical, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Germany#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:d4d9715b29f06b09b2","definition":"The various states in this country either over time or during periods of disunity and division, sometimes (inexact) inclusive of the Holy Roman Empire and Austria-Hungary's other holdings.","example":"The differences between England and the Germanies sprang from the absence or presence of ministerial interventions.","pos":"name","synonyms":["Deutschland","Germania","Dutchland","Germanland","North German Confederation","German Confederation","Confederation of the Rhine","Holy Roman Empire","First Reich","German Reich","East Francia","Austria"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"historical","register":"countable, historical","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Germany#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:20de09f568486187b5","definition":"A male given name.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":["Deutschland","Germania","Dutchland","Germanland","North German Confederation","German Confederation","Confederation of the Rhine","Holy Roman Empire","First Reich","German Reich","East Francia","Austria"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"uncommon","register":"countable, uncommon, uncountable","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Germany#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:15391c33b5dcf0357c","definition":"A surname.","example":"","pos":"name","synonyms":["Deutschland","Germania","Dutchland","Germanland","North German Confederation","German Confederation","Confederation of the Rhine